# The DOM query JS is compared byte-for-byte against the Latch extension's copy
# via SHA-256 at the WebSocket handshake. git's autocrlf would rewrite its line
# endings on checkout, changing the digest with no code change involved -- the
# handshake would then refuse every connection on a fresh clone, for a reason
# nobody would think to look for. Marking it binary stops git touching the bytes.
# The extension repo carries the matching rule; one side alone is not enough.
assistant/automation/browser/vendor/dom_query.js binary
assistant/automation/browser/vendor/dom_query.sha256 binary
